      "text": "To determine the measure of \\(\\angle ACB\\), we need to analyze the given angles and the properties of the geometric figure. The given angles are \\( \\angle BAD = 93^\\circ \\) and \\( \\angle ABC = 130^\\circ \\). We need to find the measure of \\( \\angle ACB \\).\n\nFirst, let's consider the triangle \\(\\triangle ABC\\). The angles in a triangle sum up to \\(180^\\circ\\). The angle \\(\\angle ABC\\) is given as \\(130^\\circ\\). Therefore, we can find the measure of \\(\\angle ACB\\) by subtracting the sum of the given angles \\(\\angle BAD\\) and \\(\\angle ABC\\) from \\(180^\\circ\\):\n\n\\[\n\\angle ACB = 180^\\circ - (\\angle ABC + \\angle BAD) = 180^\\circ - (130^\\circ + 93^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nCalculating the right-hand side, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\angle ACB = 180^\\circ - 223^\\circ + 93^\\circ - 130^\\circ = 47^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle ACB\\) is \\(\\boxed{47^\\circ}\\).\n\nTo confirm the accuracy of this calculation, we can write a Python code to verify it.\n```python\n# Given angles\nangle_BAD = 93\nangle_ABC = 130\n\n# The sum of angles in a triangle\nangle_sum_triangle = 180\n\n# Calculate the measure of angle ACB\nangle_ACB = angle_sum_triangle - (angle_BAD + angle_ABC)\nprint(angle_ACB)\n```",
